        <h2>What Kind of Farm Is This, Actually?</h2>
        <p>
          Smoky Mountain Acres is a growing family farm in Cosby, Tennessee. Our pigs, chickens, and sheep are raised as part of a pasture-based system where the land is an active part of their daily lives.
        </p>
        <p>
          That does not mean every animal eats grass all day or that pasture removes the need for good feed. It means we make room for natural behavior, pay attention to the ground, and adjust our care as animals and seasons change.
        </p>
        <p>
          This page explains what we mean when we say <a href="#pasture-raised">pasture-raised</a> and <a href="#organic-feed">organic feed</a>, so the people who visit, buy from, or follow our farm can understand the practices behind those words.
        </p>
