<section id="seasonal-care" class="about section paper-texture">
  <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up">
    <div class="row gy-4">
      <div class="col-lg-6 content">
        <h2>What Happens During Winter?</h2>
        <p>
          Pasture changes throughout the year. Spring growth, summer heat, autumn forage, and winter dormancy all affect what the land can provide.
        </p>
        <p>
          When pasture growth slows, we do not make unrealistic "grass only" claims. Sheep may rely more heavily on hay, pigs may need more supplemental feed, and chickens find fewer insects and growing plants. We adjust feeding, shelter, and pasture use to match the conditions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-6 content">
        <h2>What Does Transparency Mean Here?</h2>
        <p>
          It means describing our practices plainly and keeping claims specific. We want people to be able to ask what the animals eat, where they live, how we manage pasture, and what our use of the word "organic" does and does not mean.
        </p>
        <p>
          The farm is still growing, and our practices will keep developing with the land and animals. We would rather explain the real work, including its seasonal limits, than make the farm sound simpler or more certified than it is.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="cta-btn">Ask Us About Our Practices</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>